<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The non-credit English as a Second Language (ESL) program at Lake Tahoe Community College is designed as a series of sequential courses, ranging from Low Beginning through Advanced levels of English proficiency. The sequential curriculum, based on an integrated set of student learning outcomes, provides instruction through listening, speaking, reading, and writing.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<table class="ou-two-columns-2-1"><caption>Two Columns (2:1 Split)</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Column</th>
<th>Column</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><img src="{{f:38997866}}" alt="Learning" width="1080" height="572" />
<h6 class="snippet-spacer"><b>DO NOT EDIT THIS TEXT (content in this row will not appear on page).</b> <br />Enter the heading in the left cell, and the body that displays when you expand the row in the right cell. To add another row to the accordion, add another row to the table.</h6>
<table class="ou_accordion_2" style="height: 167px;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Accordion ID (must be unique if more than one accordion on page)</td>
<td>accordion1</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Certificate of Competency</span></td>
<td>
<p><strong>Students can start the ESL certificate program at any of the following levels:</strong><br />ESL 561A ESL Low Beginning or<br />ESL 562A ESL High Beginning or<span>&nbsp;</span><br />ESL 563A ESL Low Intermediate or<span>&nbsp;</span><br />ESL 564A ESL Intermediate or<span>&nbsp;</span><br />ESL 564B ESL High Intermediate or<span>&nbsp;</span><br />ESL 572A ESL: Conversation<br />ESL 573A ESL: Intermediate Writing</p>
<p><strong>When a student is proficient at all of the levels mentioned above, they then go on to complete the following courses to earn the certificate:</strong><br />ESL 565 ESL Advanced<span>&nbsp;</span><br />ESL 592B ESL: Pronunciation II</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Financial Aid &amp; Scholarships</td>
